{"name":"Kitsilano Cookie","hex":"#d0c8b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cookie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat, baked good which is either crisp or soft but firm.","A sweet baked good (as in the previous sense) usually having chocolate chips, fruit, nuts, etc. baked into it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send a cookie to (a user, computer, etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kitsilano","blocks":[{"text":"Kitsilano is a neighbourhood in the city of Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada. Named after Squamish chief August Jack Khatsahlano, Kitsilano is located along the southern shore of English Bay between Fairview and West Point Grey, with Burrard Street as the neighbourhood's eastern boundary, Alma Street its western boundary, and 16th Avenue its southern boundary. The area is mostly residential with two main commercial areas, West 4th Avenue and West Broadway, known for their retail stores, restaurants and organic food markets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Kits-Beach.jpg/330px-Kits-Beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitsilano","wikidata":"Q4179275"},{"title":"Cookie","blocks":[{"text":"A cookie is a sweet biscuit with high sugar and fat content. Cookie dough is softer than that used for other types of biscuit, and they are cooked longer at lower temperatures. The dough typically contains flour, sugar, egg, and some type of oil or fat. It may include other ingredients such as raisins, oats, chocolate chips, or nuts. Cookie texture varies from crisp and crunchy to soft and chewy, depending on the exact combination of ingredients and methods used to create them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg/330px-2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_c